Title: Digital System for Hospital Management

Introduction:
Hospitals face problems when patient data is written on paper. It takes time to find information.

Problem:
Doctors and nurses spend too much time searching for old patient records.

Solution:
A new computer system was made to store all patient information digitally (Electronic Health Records).
Doctors can now quickly check reports and treatment history.

Result:
- Time saved for doctors and patients
- No missing records
- Better patient care

Conclusion:
Technology helps hospitals work faster and give better service to patients.





Title: Robots in Warehouse

Introduction:
Manual work in warehouses is slow and tiring for workers.

Problem:
Orders take too long to pack and send. Mistakes happen often.

Solution:
The company used robots and conveyor belts to move and pack items automatically.

Result:
- Work became faster
- Fewer mistakes
- Less cost for the company

Conclusion:
Automation helps industries save time and money with accurate work.
